WEBVTT

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:25.940
Good morning, young lady.

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:27.230
Good morning, Tome-san.

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:33.410
Well then, let's eat.

00:01:33.410 --> 00:01:34.610
Thanks for the food.

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:37.860
The weather sure is nice today.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:40.120
Yeah.

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:50.920
Oh no!  Your undergarments!

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:53.010
I'll go grab them!

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:06.580
Did you really think you'd beat me?

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:09.560
Chiko!  What are you doing to him?

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:14.570
Shunka fell in love with a bad guy who
was trying to defeat the Detective Girls.

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:15.320
Ah!

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:18.070
T-Tome-san!

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:19.820
Huh?  You couldn't have!

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:21.250
I'm sorry.

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:23.330
I...  I...

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:26.830
I've fallen in love with Tome-san!

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.580
What?!

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:39.170
So, what do you think?

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:40.740
Uhm...

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:43.690
It's completely different from what I wrote!

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:46.600
Where the hell did the love triangle come from?!

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:50.800
But it'll never be popular in girls' magazines if it doesn't have a love story.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:55.100
Listen.  The Detective Girls are fighting for justice.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:55.650
Therefore...

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:57.740
I wonder what happens next!

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:01.690
Will it be Tome-san or Koito-san who ends up with that man?

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:03.600
I just said, that's not what it's about!

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:09.390
Are you going for a walk again today before going home?

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:10.080
Yeah.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:11.330
A walk?

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:14.110
There's a place she likes to go to.

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:16.940
Could you be having a secret love meeting with a man?!

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:18.860
N-No!

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:20.410
She's blushing!

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:21.610
Very suspicious!

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:23.540
Come on, that's impossible.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:24.520
Oh?

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:25.900
That's boring.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.580
See you tomorrow!

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:29.530
Bye!

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:30.390
Take care.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:41.410
I really enjoyed those times,

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:44.570
but these days aren't bad either.

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:12.060
Oh, hello.

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:15.060
Wow, it's unusual for someone else to be here.

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:17.870
Hello.

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:20.880
Would you mind if I stayed here too?

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:23.820
Of course not.  The more the merrier.

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:28.310
My, it sure feels nice here, doesn't it?

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:32.620
Yes.  I live very close by, but I only just recently discovered it.

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:34.680
Is that so?

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:37.400
I haven't come here for a while.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:41.590
Maybe not since they carved out the mountain.  I used to love this place.

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:47.590
When I was a child, this was forest for as far as the eye could see.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:52.320
After I started school, they rapidly started building houses here.

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:57.130
I could see this country develop before my own eyes.  Those were exciting times.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:01.340
I came here as soon as the war ended too.

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:06.820
It was shocking.  It was nothing but piles of rubble.

00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:10.580
I bet you couldn't even imagine that.

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:13.810
My apologies.

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:16.490
I was reminiscing like an old man.

00:05:16.490 --> 00:05:21.090
This place brings back all sorts of memories.

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:23.840
All sorts of memories...

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:31.450
It is the warm law of men

00:05:31.450 --> 00:05:34.850
From grapes, they make the wine

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:39.860
From coals, they make the fire

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:44.880
From kisses, they make the men

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:49.890
It is the warm law of men

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:54.620
From grapes, they make the wine

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:59.280
From coals, they make the fire

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:02.630
From kisses, they make...

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:10.640
I've never heard that before.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:12.530
What's that song called?

00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:16.640
Well...  I actually forgot all about that song.

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:22.730
Maybe this place really does bring back all sorts of memories.

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:25.180
I have to be heading back home now.

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:26.260
Oh, I see.

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:27.990
See you later then.

00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:35.160
Young lady!  Young lady...

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:37.190
I thought you'd be here.

00:06:37.190 --> 00:06:39.500
We've been looking for you.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:41.250
Tonight we make sukiyaki.

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:42.520
It's my treat.

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:46.760
Akine-san...  He's eating all his meals over at our place...

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:49.720
Come now, you're a growing child.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:52.180
Go on, eat some more meat.

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:53.550
But that's too much...

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:55.780
Just keep on eating, young lady.

00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:57.430
These days aren't bad...

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:02.700
But, I can't help but remember the old times.

00:07:15.190 --> 00:07:17.790
Koito-san, what on earth are we doing?

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:20.740
Shush.  This is a job for the Detective Girls.

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:21.670
Ah, she's coming!

00:07:36.730 --> 00:07:39.010
Oh, now I see.

00:07:39.010 --> 00:07:40.030
What?

00:07:40.030 --> 00:07:44.250
It looks like Tabata-sensei and Honda-sensei are seeing each other.

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:44.520
Huh?

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:48.220
What I mean is, they're dating.

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:51.420
One of the students saw them kissing.

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:52.890
What?!

00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:54.950
You heard them humming before, right?

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:57.700
That's a signal they use to arrange their rendezvous.

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:02.830
What I mean is, rather than saying "Can we see each other later today?",

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:04.780
they hum a song instead.

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:09.300
If the answer is yes, the other person hums the song back.

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:15.220
It's like a secret code just for the two of them.

00:08:16.210 --> 00:08:19.490
And this is a job for the Detective Girls?

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:21.510
What happened to justice?

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:27.700
What I mean is, they're supposed to be teachers upholding the sacred art of instruction, so we can't just let them fool around on the job!

00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:29.400
Denouncing that would be justice...

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:30.570
So what's the verdict?

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:33.710
They're dating, aren't they?

00:08:33.710 --> 00:08:34.570
Of course!

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:37.250
I witnessed it with my own eyes.

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:38.640
First, she...

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:44.580
It would be great if Twenty Faces would come see me when I sing that song.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:52.030
Oh, young lady.

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:54.520
Are you going to that hill again today?

00:08:54.520 --> 00:08:58.830
If you don't mind, I'd appreciate if you would keep me company again.

00:08:59.690 --> 00:09:00.940
Well, today, I...

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:04.520
I have something I need to talk to you about.

00:09:06.050 --> 00:09:10.590
It was no coincidence that we met on that hill yesterday.

00:09:11.850 --> 00:09:14.050
Oh, I haven't introduced myself yet.

00:09:14.670 --> 00:09:17.040
I'm Kakishima Kouhei.

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:18.570
I'm a college professor.

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:20.030
Or, rather, I was.

00:09:21.380 --> 00:09:24.880
That man you all call Twenty Faces...

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:26.790
...was my student.

00:09:31.910 --> 00:09:33.940
His teacher...

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:36.010
He knows about his past.

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:38.510
He understands him.

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:45.140
The reason I invited you here today is because there's something I want to learn from you.

00:09:45.690 --> 00:09:49.550
From you, the one they call the Daughter of Twenty Faces.

00:09:49.550 --> 00:09:53.280
I think it's for your own good.

00:09:54.430 --> 00:09:57.290
He was a brilliant student.

00:09:58.130 --> 00:10:01.240
He was a superb researcher from the moment I met him.

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:07.280
That's why when I was putting together my own research team,

00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:09.890
I invited him without hesitation.

00:10:09.890 --> 00:10:14.960
We didn't restrict ourselves to specific lines of research and allowed for free discussion.

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:19.040
In no time at all, he became the leader of the team.

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:22.200
But, after all, it was a student organization,

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:27.560
so we quickly exhausted our funds, and had to halt the research.

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:30.810
And then...

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:32.270
The war started.

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:36.410
I figured I'd be too busy to even consider research,

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:42.070
but he came to me with an offer of considerable research funds for a military project.

00:10:45.230 --> 00:10:48.130
"Watch, listen, and think for yourself."

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:51.290
That was his doctrine.

00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:57.890
However, with a doctrine like that, he had a tendency to be self-righteous.

00:10:57.890 --> 00:11:00.320
When our defeat in the war was definite,

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:05.790
he felt that the data should belong to him, so he burned down our facility.

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:10.470
And, when he surfaced for the second time,

00:11:10.470 --> 00:11:13.860
he was being called Twenty Faces.

00:11:16.510 --> 00:11:22.860
We were researching a technique to provide unlimited electrical power to an entire city.

00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:29.320
Unfortunately, that power could also be used to destroy an entire city.

00:11:29.320 --> 00:11:33.650
It can take on an unseen form, allowing for control of unbelievable amounts of energy.

00:11:35.520 --> 00:11:37.630
Unseen form?

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:41.400
I'm searching for all the research he did.

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:47.350
And then I heard a rumor that the Daughter of Twenty Faces carries his legacy.

00:11:49.290 --> 00:11:53.180
He used you as his decoy.

00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:54.400
I'm no decoy!

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:56.860
Of course, he didn't have any other options.

00:11:56.860 --> 00:12:03.280
However, he's hiding behind you and trying to do something monumental.

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:09.970
You're just a pawn in his plan to cause another huge disaster.

00:12:13.170 --> 00:12:17.340
He didn't take me under his wing for that reason.

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:21.740
Anyone who gets involved with him becomes enchanted with him.

00:12:21.740 --> 00:12:23.430
And then they come to misfortune.

00:12:29.020 --> 00:12:31.160
I want to save you.

00:12:31.720 --> 00:12:36.770
For that reason, please leave me in care of everything he's entrusted to you.

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:38.210
Entrusted to me?

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:42.150
I don't want you to be exposed to any more danger.

00:12:45.980 --> 00:12:49.990
I know you must be bewildered hearing all this at once.

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:52.760
Well then, I'll come see you again.

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:03.620
Am I his decoy?

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:08.240
Is what that professor said the truth?

00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:10.040
I have to think.

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:11.220
But...

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:16.690
I don't know anything about what he was like before he became Twenty Faces.

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:20.210
Unfathomable energy...

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:25.700
People believe I know that secret and that's what they're after.

00:13:26.620 --> 00:13:29.740
He knew that would happen.

00:13:33.270 --> 00:13:35.950
But what did he entrust to me?

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:38.960
Young lady.

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:44.800
Please don't think about Twenty Faces anymore.

00:13:48.100 --> 00:13:53.720
From the day I came to your home, I made up my mind to stay with you until you come of age.

00:13:54.210 --> 00:13:55.660
Tome-san...

00:13:55.660 --> 00:14:01.320
Until the day you were able to handle your inheritance on your own.

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:05.400
You are the legitimate heiress of your family.

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:10.820
Twenty Faces is an untrustworthy man that has no connection to that whatsoever.

00:14:12.860 --> 00:14:17.590
I understand that you went through some very emotional times with him,

00:14:17.590 --> 00:14:22.520
but anyone they call the Mystery Man with Twenty Faces is not a man we can trust!

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:29.180
I can't just sit silently by and watch your mind become clouded because of a man like that!

00:14:31.330 --> 00:14:32.680
Tome-san...

00:14:34.950 --> 00:14:35.680
I understand.

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:39.230
Tome-san is worried about me.

00:15:07.890 --> 00:15:10.530
It seems he's found another woman.

00:15:10.530 --> 00:15:14.690
And so apparently Tabata-sensei's been dumped.

00:15:14.690 --> 00:15:16.060
I feel bad for her.

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:19.060
He didn't look like the type to do something like that.

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:21.250
Honda-sensei is a real jerk.

00:15:22.950 --> 00:15:25.090
How can you be sure he's to blame?

00:15:26.680 --> 00:15:28.990
There might be various circumstances at play here.

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:32.740
What's this, Mikamo-san?  You're talking like an adult!

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:41.750
You're just a pawn in his plan to cause another huge disaster.

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:43.680
He's wrong.

00:15:43.680 --> 00:15:44.760
But...

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:52.810
It is the warm law of men

00:15:53.740 --> 00:15:58.080
From grapes, they make the wine

00:15:58.080 --> 00:16:00.050
That's "Bonne Justice", isn't it?

00:16:00.050 --> 00:16:01.570
"Bonne Justice"?

00:16:01.570 --> 00:16:04.340
Oh, you were singing it without knowing its name?

00:16:04.340 --> 00:16:06.440
It's a poem by Paul Éluard.

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:07.520
Éluard?

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:14.910
It's a great poem.  It's about the laws of men:  warm, harsh, and kind.

00:16:17.630 --> 00:16:20.660
So I guess you've heard the rumors about me, huh?

00:16:21.910 --> 00:16:23.640
But...

00:16:23.640 --> 00:16:27.390
Even if it stings now, it'll all be a pleasurable memory one day.

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:30.070
(It is the warm law of men)
C'est la chaude loi des hommes

00:16:30.070 --> 00:16:32.540
(From grapes, they make the wine)
Du raisin ils font du vin

00:16:32.540 --> 00:16:34.970
(From coals, they make the fire)
Du charbon ils font du feu

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:37.430
(From kisses, they make the men)
Des baisers ils font des hommes

00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:38.010
C'est la dure loi des hommes

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:40.630
(It is the harsh law of men)
C'est la dure loi des hommes

00:16:40.630 --> 00:16:43.850
(They keep themselves intact despite)
Se garder intact malgré

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:45.940
(The wars and the misery)
Les guerres et la misère

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:48.710
(Despite the dangers of death)
Malgré les dangers de mort

00:16:49.310 --> 00:16:52.170
Grapes... they make... wine.

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:56.410
Coals... they make... fire.

00:17:02.330 --> 00:17:04.530
From grapes, they make the wine.

00:17:04.530 --> 00:17:06.520
From coals, they make the fire.

00:17:06.520 --> 00:17:09.140
From kisses, they make the men.

00:17:09.140 --> 00:17:11.950
That is the warm law of men.

00:17:11.950 --> 00:17:17.030
They keep themselves intact despite the wars and the misery.

00:17:17.030 --> 00:17:19.410
Despite the dangers of death.

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:22.200
That is the harsh law of men.

00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:24.240
They turn water into light.

00:17:24.240 --> 00:17:26.250
They turn dreams into reality.

00:17:26.250 --> 00:17:28.400
They turn enemies into brothers.

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:30.980
That is the kind law of man.

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:37.530
Could what he entrusted to me be inside this poem?

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:38.990
Or in the song?

00:17:55.970 --> 00:17:59.190
Well, I'm afraid I've never heard that song before.

00:17:59.190 --> 00:18:00.450
I see.

00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:17.900
He's so fast!

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:27.870
I'll have a leg up on the swing!

00:18:43.700 --> 00:18:45.330
Your role is over.

00:18:47.990 --> 00:18:49.560
I'm sorry for you.

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:50.940
I'm told you're not needed anymore.

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:54.170
Chiko!

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:55.420
Ken-niichan!

00:18:57.130 --> 00:18:57.650
Chiko!

00:18:58.270 --> 00:18:59.390
Are you all right?

00:19:02.070 --> 00:19:03.660
Who was that?

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:05.390
I don't know.

00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:12.590
I tried asking around about the Boss, but couldn't find out anything.

00:19:12.590 --> 00:19:13.420
I see.

00:19:13.890 --> 00:19:15.280
Be careful.

00:19:15.280 --> 00:19:18.460
That guy from before might show up again.

00:19:18.460 --> 00:19:19.070
Yeah.

00:19:21.900 --> 00:19:23.450
Thanks for taking me home.

00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:24.990
See you!

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:31.440
I have to change before Tome-san sees me.

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:40.700
Did Twenty Faces order that guy from before to attack me?

00:19:42.210 --> 00:19:43.310
But...

00:19:43.310 --> 00:19:46.660
He would never kill me.

00:19:50.350 --> 00:19:52.830
Maybe I was a little too harsh on the young lady.

00:19:54.010 --> 00:20:00.340
But if she could understand that there's someone here to care for her, I think that she'd...

00:20:02.820 --> 00:20:03.860
I'm...

00:20:04.490 --> 00:20:06.580
...putting my trust in Twenty Faces.

00:20:12.810 --> 00:20:16.880
That man knows something more about Twenty Faces.

00:20:17.590 --> 00:20:19.130
If I want to get closer to Twenty Faces,

00:20:20.080 --> 00:20:21.940
I must accept his invitation.

00:20:36.870 --> 00:20:37.880
Oh no!

00:20:38.950 --> 00:20:39.900
This is terrible!

00:20:41.070 --> 00:20:43.130
Aw shucks...

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:56.520
Let's get going now please.

00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:03.950
I'll make it to Twenty Faces this time.

00:21:04.640 --> 00:21:05.850
I've made up my mind.

00:21:06.600 --> 00:21:08.410
Please forgive me, Tome-san.
